Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 21:00:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07156/11362] [outer-loop] exp5709: Ternary Bonsai (3rd-party
 CUDA fork) reinduction A/B (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5599-3)

Operator-directed follow-up to exp5705: try prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-27B-gguf
(~1.71 bits/weight ternary quant of Qwen3.6-27B) on CUDA. Required building
a bespoke third-party llama.cpp fork (PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp) since standard
llama.cpp can't load its Q2_0_g128 tensor type. Pre-integration audit found
no dedicated ternary CUDA kernel files via grep, raising a real concern
about silent CPU fallback -- empirically this did not materialize: built
clean, loaded on GPU 1 (RTX 3090, 22.5GB real GPU memory), generated
coherent text at 67.5 tok/s.

Real reinduction result on the same lp85 methodology as exp5599/exp5705:
reached a level-up, completed the full attempt in 212.948s (11x faster
than exp5705's Q8_0/iGPU run). Got further too -- round 1 produced valid
parseable code, rejected as degenerate_goal_predicate (semantic failure,
not syntax failure) -- before failing the refactor retry. Verdict:
plans less reliably than the frozen 9B (0/1 vs 1/3 historical).

Fourth independent measurement (Q4 Qwen, Q8_0 Gemma, ternary Bonsai, all
vs the 9B) pointing the same direction across 3 quant schemes, 2 model
families, 2 serving stacks, 2 hardware classes. Confounds disclosed, not
hidden. Frozen live-submission generator remains unchanged.

Note: the experiment script + results json were independently swept into
a concurrent conductor commit (8e5d87b95) via its own git add -A -- byte-
identical, verified before this commit. This commit adds the spec write-up,
known-issues entry, and test file only.
